g/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc that has an inline // comment and overrides a shipped id: before, 0 user rows; after, does the override replace the shipped row?"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Before this change, a user extension with any inline // comment, a comma-comment-closer sequence or CRLF line endings plus inline comments parsed to 0 rows, so the shipped menu was used unchanged (docs/menu.md: a broken extension silently drops every user entry). After the change such a file parses, and its entries override defaults per key (SW-REQ-260922-7NPE). This is the PR's purpose. Still, a user whose extension was stale but invisible will see its entries appear on upgrade. Bounded consequence: rows the user authored; nothing runs without a selection.","refs":[{"id":"docs/menu.md","kind":"file","line":15},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-7NPE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260928-C8W1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: do user extensions that were silently ignored before now load and override shipped entries?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Upgrade witness: an inline-commented user extension that overrides a shipped id\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"check":"known_issue_sibling_disposition","position":"plausibly_pr_caused"},"type":"check_attribution"},"detail":"Gate delta: introduced (passed at baseline run-a1d72522). Setting KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMA-IN-STRING / -ARRAY-ROOT / -INLINE-COMMENT to fixed (dogfood proof work, 83b9a722) asks for a disposition of the open KIs with the same kill_domain=parsing: KI-MENU-JSONC-STRIP-GAPS (/* */ block comments; still reproduces at the evaluated tree, reviewer-checked), KI-MENU-ITEMS-KEY-AMBIGUITY (parseMenuJsonc's `items` wrapper check, MenuModel.js:102, unchanged by the PR) and KI-MENU-KEYBINDINGS-CSV-DESC-COM